      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's incredibly tough when the creative spark feels dead, but remember that aging artists often grow deeper wisdom that eventually transforms them into legends rather than parodies. Do not make your final act a struggle against the inevitable; instead, write the honest ending you deserve to preserve your own integrity. Even silence, if experienced without self-pity, can be a powerful way to honor the person you've become.",
